  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA 26/2018 Relief and Early Recovery Assistance to people affected by Typhoon Mangkhut</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Typhoon Mangkhut (local name: Ompong) made landfall in Baggao, Cagayan 15 September 2018. According to UN-OCHA&#x2019;s flash update (September 19, 2018), more than one million individuals are affected in Regions I, II, III, CALABARZON (Cavite, Batangas, Laguna, Rizal and Quezon provinces), National Caritas Region, and the Cordillera Administrative Region (CAR). The same report reveals that more than 184,000 people are displaced. Of which, 61,000 are still in 471 evacuation centers and more than 87,000 individuals are staying with host families. 

NASSA/Caritas Philippines&apos;s response will not only be providing emergency relief assistance, but will ensure that the vital elements of community-managed disaster risk reduction like community participation, accountability, disaster and capacity mapping, and contingency planning, are integrated in the appeal implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
